      "scope": "in_scope",
      "statement": "Staunton's conjecture is true: for every $n\\geq1$,\n\\[\n a_n=2^{b_n-2}.\n\\]\nMore explicitly, if $s_2(m)$ denotes the number of ones in the binary\nexpansion of $m$, then\n\\begin{equation}\n a_n=2^{\\,2n-1-s_2(n+1)},\\qquad\n b_n=2n+1-s_2(n+1).\n\\end{equation}\nThe displayed formula for $b_n$ also holds at $n=0$.",
      "status": "preparing",
